WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.680
University of Guelph research shows raising entire male pigs could cut Canadian swine greenhouse gas emissions by 11.2% per kilogram of carcass weight. This is Environmental Intelligence, episode 78. The growth and feed figures behind that cut come next, then the manure and export context, then the checks and nutrient plan actually has to make. The University of Guelph Department of Animal Biosciences, in work carried by Innovation News Network, finds that entire males set against

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.260
castrates, produce less manure, put less nitrogen in that manure, and eat less feed.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.720
Those three shifts land in greenhouse gas accounting and in nutrient management on Canadian

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.920
swine operations, so the performance numbers belong against provincial reporting expectations

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.540
this week.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.980
Worldwide pork production already exceeds 100 million tons a year.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:57.920
Canada sends approximately 75% of its pork to export markets, and in 2021 it shipped more

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:04.800
than 1.5 million tons, valued at roughly $5 billion, ranking third among global exporters

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.420
on United States Department of Agriculture figures.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.980
Swine production is the second largest contributor to livestock sector greenhouse gas emissions

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.040
at 707.3 million tons of carbon dioxide equivalent worldwide.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:25.400
Canadian Swine operations contributed 6.7 million tons of carbon dioxide equivalent as of 2001,

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.820
1, and manure accounts for 81% of total greenhouse gas emissions from swine systems.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.620
The comparison is castrated barrels against entire males.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:42.300
Entire males show 13% faster growth, 20% higher lean yield, 14% better feed conversion,

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:48.480
and 9.5% lower feed intake, and those shifts are what cut manure volume and pull nitrogen

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.140
out of it.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:55.660
Scaled up, the Canadian total is an estimated 0.75 million tons of carbon dioxide equivalent

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.280
a year, against 39.6 million tons worldwide.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.940
Less nitrogen in the manure also lowers the risk of leaching into water bodies.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:09.120
Ontario Ministry of Agriculture, food and agribusiness figures put feed costs in the

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.100
grower finisher phase at approximately $224 per ton of pork produced.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:19.560
At current prices, the lower feed intake alone could deliver nearly 87 million Canadian

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:25.500
dollars in annual savings for Canadian producers, if half of the 12.6 million market hogs

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.960
recorded in January 2026 are raised as entire males.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:35.880
Feeding expenses on that export volume reached $336 million, and the same production shift

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.980
would cut into that bill.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:41.880
Routine castration of male piglets is still common in many countries because it prevents

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:47.460
bore taint, even though it raises animal welfare concerns and lowers overall system efficiency.

00:02:48.537 --> 00:02:53.417
Minuer nutrient profiles are the first place the efficiency metrics meet a plan, where

00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:56.337
feed conversion and growth point to lower manure nitrogen.

00:02:56.957 --> 00:03:01.617
Nitrogen loading calculations need to move with them, and a provincial nutrient management

00:03:01.617 --> 00:03:05.457
plan may need an update once the barn actually shifts to entire males.

00:03:06.177 --> 00:03:09.637
Storage and land application permits are the constraint on volume.

00:03:09.637 --> 00:03:14.497
time. Any drop in manure has to still fit what the relevant province has already authorized.

00:03:15.097 --> 00:03:19.357
The basis for the revised factors should be written down so later compliance reporting

00:03:19.357 --> 00:03:24.647
can point straight at the University of Guelph performance data. Greenhouse gas inventory

00:03:24.647 --> 00:03:29.787
assumptions need the same pass on any operation weighing that shift, including whether the

00:03:29.787 --> 00:03:35.007
Canadian annual reduction projection changes corporate sustainability reporting or a provincial

00:03:35.007 --> 00:03:40.707
greenhouse gas offset calculation. That covers today's environmental intelligence. If you

